# codespell config — also picked up by BuildFlow's codespell step for options
# BuildFlow does not pass on its CLI (--skip/--quiet-level ARE overridden by
# BuildFlow, so file-level noise is handled via ignore-words-list below).
#
# ignore-words-list entries are all verified false positives:
#   te, ue, ore, Te, Ue, BU, Ot, ot, vEw, PtD — camelCase identifier fragments
#   (htmx.min.js vendored bundle, SVG diagrams, lockfile integrity hashes)
#   MapPin  — icon name (icons.IconPin family)
#   wantIn  — Go test variable in examples/demo/sse_test.go
#   devlop, trough — substrings of pnpm-lock.yaml integrity hashes (lockfiles
#   are never hand-edited)
#   STARTTED — historical status-report typo, fixed in place 2026-09-08
#   crasher — deliberate term in incident reports ("a crasher")
#   pre-select* / re-declares / pre-empt* — hyphenated house style
ignore-words-list =
    te, ue, ore, Te, Ue, BU, Ot, ot, vEw, PtD,
    MapPin, wantIn, devlop, trough, STARTTED, crasher,
    pre-select, pre-selected, pre-selects, pre-selecting, Pre-select,
    pre-empt, pre-empts, Pre-emptive, re-declares
